- F-279 **Under walk an `Array2` or `Array3` based above zero slices like a 0-based one, except a shifted `Array2`.** `Array2.subarray` and `Array3.subarray` hand their 0-based views the offset less the base, and `Array3`'s `[:]` passes its base, as `Array1`'s do. A shifted `Array2` is the exception: `SubArray2`'s own `subarray` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:3083`) subtracts the output base instead of its own, so its slices read the wrong elements and its shifts fail (row 808: its cases, the one-line repair and a way around). Gated by `tests/Array*SliceAtNonzeroBase`; row 808's expected failure is `tests/XXXArray2ShiftedSlice`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-slices-list-equality/REPORT.md`, sections 1 and 5.
  from: compile-ladder/rung-slices-list-equality/REPORT.md, "1. What changed and why"; note: pilot round 1, case 3 (a defect beside its property): the shifted `Array2`'s defect (a slice reads the wrong elements, a shift of a slice, a column, a row or a shifted `Array2` ends in `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`) to row 808, which holds it; the line `:3083` kept until row 808's notes give today's line (they give `:2828`, the report `:2816`); the other source lines (`:2999`, `:3401`, `:3380`, `:2711`) to this history and the report.

- F-157 **An array is a trait with `get` and `put`, and a view is an object that implements it over other storage; this is the language's own idiom for a view of a runtime shape, as the library's own `TransposedMatrix` is.** Under walk, a subtype of `Matrix` that overrides `mul` gets its own product through the library's `Matrix` juxtaposition and `DOT`, which forward to `mul`. It needs no api line, since walk dispatches the method on the receiver's run-time type; the override was measured under walk only. Under walk the library's own views cost more than a user's: its row slice `m[i,:]` five times a six-line user view (row 298), and its product through a diagonal held as a plain `Matrix` view 13 to 63 times a row-scaling operator (row 299, whose 54 the probe's timings correct). Detail: `reviews/c4-flatarrays-review.md` section 1 (the idiom); `run-c4/probes/vocabulary/diag-override.md`, "Result" (the override) and "Timings against row 299" (the ratios).
