- F-102 **An `XXX*.fss` in the interpreter corpus is a gated expected-failure test.** `SystemJUTest` marks a file of `ProjectFortress/tests/` whose name starts with `XXX` as one that must fail, and the suite goes red when it passes. Without a `.test` file the harness reads only that the program fails, not its message, and no gate stage compares what a test prints with an earlier run. The test needs a `.test` file only to name a refusal at load by its `load_` keys, as any program of `tests/` does (F-383, what counts as a refusal at load). An `XXX` test that imports an api with its component, as `XXXImportImportCollision.fss` does, takes them from `ProjectFortress/test_library/`, so it needs no new api folder. The compiled corpora's rule differs (F-103). Read in the code: `tests/unit_tests/FileTests.java`.
